<details class="permission-explainer"><summary><MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.Info" Size="Size.Small" aria-hidden="true"/> Permissions and consent explained</summary>
<div class="permission-comparison">
<section><strong>Delegated · with a user</strong><div class="permission-route">User + App → API</div><p>Scopes describe what the app may do for the signed-in user. Both the app’s permission and the user’s access must allow the operation.</p><p><strong>Consent:</strong> user consent when allowed; administrator consent when required by the permission or tenant policy.</p></section>
<section><strong>Application · without a user</strong><div class="permission-route">App → API</div><p>App roles grant access to the application itself, for example a background service. No signed-in user is involved.</p><p><strong>Consent:</strong> an administrator grants application permissions. Managed identities use resource role assignments.</p></section>
</div><p>An API can support both, with separate scopes and app roles. Your selected scenario determines which to configure.</p><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/identity-platform/permissions-consent-overview" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Learn: permissions and consent ↗</a></details>
